WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.339 --> 00:00:02.757
- Good morning Believe
Nation, today's message is

00:00:02.757 --> 00:00:04.659
work the hardest.

00:00:04.659 --> 00:00:06.299
Over to you Wayne Gretzky.

00:00:06.299 --> 00:00:08.557
(rooster crowing)

00:00:08.557 --> 00:00:11.168
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:11.168 --> 00:00:13.919
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:13.919 --> 00:00:18.077
♫ I wake up every morning ♫

00:00:18.077 --> 00:00:20.365
- [Wayne] Professional
sports isn't much different

00:00:20.365 --> 00:00:21.526
than the real world.

00:00:21.526 --> 00:00:23.695
The players who love it
the most, and the players

00:00:23.695 --> 00:00:25.391
who work the hardest.

00:00:25.391 --> 00:00:28.086
The players who put in
the biggest commitment

00:00:28.086 --> 00:00:31.269
they're the ones who ultimately
are successful as athletes.

00:00:31.269 --> 00:00:33.135
And then when they go into
the real world, the business

00:00:33.135 --> 00:00:36.710
world, those are the athletes
who become successful

00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:38.503
in a whole different venture.

00:00:38.503 --> 00:00:40.670
So, there's a very similar

00:00:41.665 --> 00:00:44.498
sort of mindset to whatever it is,

00:00:45.466 --> 00:00:46.895
and the good lord blessed me.

00:00:46.895 --> 00:00:48.182
I was fortunate enough
to play in the National

00:00:48.182 --> 00:00:49.145
Hockey League.

00:00:49.145 --> 00:00:51.502
Why I was chosen, I don't know.

00:00:51.502 --> 00:00:54.003
When you focus all your
attention on being the best

00:00:54.003 --> 00:00:55.698
player you can become.

00:00:55.698 --> 00:00:57.203
And that's a full-time job.

00:00:57.203 --> 00:00:59.500
I mean, you don't have time to think about

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:02.060
life after hockey, life during hockey.

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:04.085
If you want to be the
best athlete you can be

00:01:04.085 --> 00:01:06.046
your focus is just doing that

00:01:06.046 --> 00:01:07.520
and playing the game of hockey.

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:09.838
- The people who win work the hardest

00:01:09.838 --> 00:01:11.301
because they love what they do.

00:01:11.301 --> 00:01:13.570
They put in the hours and
the hours and the hours

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:15.544
and the hours for days and days and days

00:01:15.544 --> 00:01:17.054
and weeks and weeks and weeks

00:01:17.054 --> 00:01:18.931
and months and months and months.

00:01:18.931 --> 00:01:20.308
And years and years and years.

00:01:20.308 --> 00:01:21.235
Because they love it.

00:01:21.235 --> 00:01:22.842
Because it's not work for them.

00:01:22.842 --> 00:01:25.119
The only way you're going
to be willing to put in

00:01:25.119 --> 00:01:27.780
the work that is necessary to win,

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:30.241
to be the best in your industry

00:01:30.241 --> 00:01:32.125
the only way you're going to
put in that amount of work

00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:34.955
is because, you love what you're doing.

00:01:34.955 --> 00:01:36.348
(gentle music)

00:01:36.348 --> 00:01:38.506
And if you don't, you're going to lose.

00:01:38.506 --> 00:01:40.545
'Cause there's going to be
somebody who will love it,

00:01:40.545 --> 00:01:42.050
who loves it more than you

00:01:42.050 --> 00:01:43.123
and will crush you.

00:01:43.123 --> 00:01:46.621
And you'll be not even a
number two, you'll be mediocre

00:01:46.621 --> 00:01:48.532
because there's lots of
people who love what they do.

00:01:48.532 --> 00:01:50.878
And there's lots of people
grinding it and working hard.

00:01:50.878 --> 00:01:52.650
If you are looking at your
calendar, like open up

00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:54.792
your calendar, look what
you're going to do today

00:01:54.792 --> 00:01:56.492
or look at what you're doing tomorrow.

00:01:56.492 --> 00:01:57.325
What's on the schedule?

00:01:57.325 --> 00:01:59.067
If you're looking at
it and you're like, ah,

00:01:59.067 --> 00:02:01.780
I've got to do all these things.

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:03.710
If that's your reaction

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:05.853
you might be in the wrong business.

00:02:05.853 --> 00:02:08.182
Now if it's a one-off
thing, if it's a one day

00:02:08.182 --> 00:02:09.857
you got to deal with the government,

00:02:09.857 --> 00:02:12.198
or it's something, fine.

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:14.476
But if that's daily, if that's consistent,

00:02:14.476 --> 00:02:16.138
if that's always happening,

00:02:16.138 --> 00:02:19.001
if you continue to look at
your calendar and you're

00:02:19.001 --> 00:02:21.418
upset and depressed and angry

00:02:22.683 --> 00:02:24.483
you're in the wrong business.

00:02:24.483 --> 00:02:25.316
The work

00:02:26.889 --> 00:02:30.438
should feel like something
exciting to go and do.

00:02:30.438 --> 00:02:32.302
Where other people might
jump into your schedule

00:02:32.302 --> 00:02:33.797
and say, "That's crazy.

00:02:33.797 --> 00:02:35.253
"I could never do that."

00:02:35.253 --> 00:02:37.417
That's great, that's why you're
not crushing it like I am.

00:02:37.417 --> 00:02:39.244
Like, go crush it in your field.

00:02:39.244 --> 00:02:41.179
Go do your thing.

00:02:41.179 --> 00:02:43.734
As an example, here's
one change that I've made

00:02:43.734 --> 00:02:45.465
to my YouTube channel.

00:02:45.465 --> 00:02:48.592
You may have noticed this month

00:02:48.592 --> 00:02:51.084
the video series looked
a little bit different.

00:02:51.084 --> 00:02:53.998
I'm working with a videographer, Jason.

00:02:53.998 --> 00:02:56.013
And the only way we can
make this thing work was

00:02:56.013 --> 00:02:57.523
if we did it on one day.

00:02:57.523 --> 00:03:00.579
So I used to film my videos once a week.

00:03:00.579 --> 00:03:02.723
On a Wednesday, for the week.

00:03:02.723 --> 00:03:04.494
And Jason works by the day, so,

00:03:04.494 --> 00:03:05.988
"Okay, you know what, I
want to increase the quality

00:03:05.988 --> 00:03:06.821
"of the videos.

00:03:06.821 --> 00:03:07.664
"I want them to look more Hollywood."

00:03:07.664 --> 00:03:08.777
Do we look more Hollywood?

00:03:08.777 --> 00:03:09.610
Is it looking nice?

00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:10.443
Do you guys like the quality?

00:03:10.443 --> 00:03:12.540
Give a thumbs for Jason
down in the comments.

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:15.133
And the way to make it work
was to do it once a month.

00:03:15.133 --> 00:03:17.974
And so, I'm sitting here filming my videos

00:03:17.974 --> 00:03:18.970
for the month.

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:22.533
We're doing like 70 videos in one day.

00:03:22.533 --> 00:03:23.861
Grinding them through.

00:03:23.861 --> 00:03:26.047
I've got two extra large coffees.

00:03:26.047 --> 00:03:27.478
I got one sitting behind here

00:03:27.478 --> 00:03:29.595
I'm half way through that.

00:03:29.595 --> 00:03:32.216
And here's a thing, to make this work

00:03:32.216 --> 00:03:33.995
it's a lot of extra pressure on my team

00:03:33.995 --> 00:03:36.696
to get a lot of things
ready and sooner and faster.

00:03:36.696 --> 00:03:39.256
Right, so my team's
been working extra hard

00:03:39.256 --> 00:03:41.195
to get it ready for this one time

00:03:41.195 --> 00:03:43.497
and if we continue it,
it's their usual job.

00:03:43.497 --> 00:03:45.206
It's not as stressful or hard.

00:03:45.206 --> 00:03:47.419
I'm thinking about them.

00:03:47.419 --> 00:03:49.597
I don't want them to stress out too much.

00:03:49.597 --> 00:03:52.120
But really, the person who
has it the hardest is me.

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:54.296
Because for me, it's not just

00:03:54.296 --> 00:03:55.421
a one-off thing.

00:03:55.421 --> 00:03:56.962
This is now going to be every month.

00:03:56.962 --> 00:03:59.093
Like, do I have the ability

00:03:59.093 --> 00:04:00.807
to stay "on",

00:04:00.807 --> 00:04:02.917
to have energy for an entire day?

00:04:02.917 --> 00:04:05.599
Can I get through making 70 videos

00:04:05.599 --> 00:04:06.680
in a single day?

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:07.518
I don't know.

00:04:07.518 --> 00:04:09.286
But when Jason and I are
on email we're trying

00:04:09.286 --> 00:04:11.423
to figure this out,

00:04:11.423 --> 00:04:13.806
and I look at how hard it was going to be

00:04:13.806 --> 00:04:16.910
for me to do, to be on
camera for that long.

00:04:16.910 --> 00:04:18.771
I'm like, I got to do this.

00:04:18.771 --> 00:04:19.975
This is awesome.

00:04:19.975 --> 00:04:21.038
(laughs)

00:04:21.038 --> 00:04:23.935
I might crash and burn and
like it doesn't work out

00:04:23.935 --> 00:04:26.597
and it totally fails
and I can't handle the

00:04:26.597 --> 00:04:30.174
the length and the
time, but I want to try.

00:04:30.174 --> 00:04:32.963
Where so many people have
a hard time making one

00:04:32.963 --> 00:04:34.796
to two videos a month.

00:04:35.803 --> 00:04:38.632
Here, we are making 70 in a day.

00:04:38.632 --> 00:04:40.491
Crushing it all down.

00:04:40.491 --> 00:04:42.313
And I love it.

00:04:42.313 --> 00:04:45.253
It's hardest on me versus
anybody else on my team.

00:04:45.253 --> 00:04:46.412
But I'm not even thinking about it because

00:04:46.412 --> 00:04:48.142
I love the challenge.

00:04:48.142 --> 00:04:50.423
I love the ability to
work that hard and see

00:04:50.423 --> 00:04:51.606
if I can do it.

00:04:51.606 --> 00:04:53.825
And see if it makes sense
for what we're trying to do.

00:04:53.825 --> 00:04:54.706
What do you guys think?

00:04:54.706 --> 00:04:56.573
Do you like these videos lke this?

00:04:56.573 --> 00:04:58.003
Do you want more of it?

00:04:58.003 --> 00:04:59.571
Let me know, leave a comment.

00:04:59.571 --> 00:05:01.428
And so, in thinking
about that I don't think

00:05:01.428 --> 00:05:03.491
that I'm super special, by the way.

00:05:03.491 --> 00:05:05.670
I just found the thing that I love doing.

00:05:05.670 --> 00:05:08.340
I'm willing to put in this
kind of hustle and work

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:09.685
because I love making the videos,

00:05:09.685 --> 00:05:12.583
because I want to create
more and better content

00:05:12.583 --> 00:05:13.524
for you guys.

00:05:13.524 --> 00:05:15.740
You could put in that same
amount of drive, energy,

00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:18.690
hustle that I'm doing
today in your business.

00:05:18.690 --> 00:05:20.827
But it's not going to happen
if you look at your schedule

00:05:20.827 --> 00:05:23.301
and like, go like this.

00:05:23.301 --> 00:05:24.957
I was looking at my schedule last night

00:05:24.957 --> 00:05:26.408
and like, I'm so excited about tomorrow.

00:05:26.408 --> 00:05:27.507
I'm so excited about tomorrow.

00:05:27.507 --> 00:05:28.782
It's so good, I can see how it goes

00:05:28.782 --> 00:05:30.072
try to crush it.

00:05:30.072 --> 00:05:31.341
Right, and again

00:05:31.341 --> 00:05:33.984
not every day is going
to be super amazing.

00:05:33.984 --> 00:05:37.116
But you should love the
work that you do net net.

00:05:37.116 --> 00:05:39.505
You should be excited about
the day that is ahead,

00:05:39.505 --> 00:05:41.835
net net, and not feeling sad,

00:05:41.835 --> 00:05:43.768
depressed, angry, frustrated

00:05:43.768 --> 00:05:45.367
about the work that you have to do.

00:05:45.367 --> 00:05:47.938
The people who win work
the hardest because

00:05:47.938 --> 00:05:49.368
they love what they do.

00:05:49.368 --> 00:05:51.288
So the question today I'm curious,

00:05:51.288 --> 00:05:54.567
do you look forward to
the day that you have

00:05:54.567 --> 00:05:55.544
tomorrow?

00:05:55.544 --> 00:05:57.055
Look at your schedule tomorrow,

00:05:57.055 --> 00:05:58.312
look at what's on the calendar.

00:05:58.312 --> 00:06:00.123
Are you excited about that day?

00:06:00.123 --> 00:06:01.581
I know it's just a snapshot

00:06:01.581 --> 00:06:03.172
but I want to know for tomorrow,

00:06:03.172 --> 00:06:05.690
are you excited and what's
the most interesting

00:06:05.690 --> 00:06:07.867
and exciting thing that
you have on your list?

00:06:07.867 --> 00:06:09.068
Leave it down in the comments below

00:06:09.068 --> 00:06:10.752
and we'll join in the discussion.

00:06:10.752 --> 00:06:12.479
I also want to give a
quick shout out to Chase.

00:06:12.479 --> 00:06:13.992
Chase, thank you so much
for picking up a copy

00:06:13.992 --> 00:06:15.677
of my book, Year One Word.

00:06:15.677 --> 00:06:17.418
It really really really means a lot to me

00:06:17.418 --> 00:06:18.639
and I hope you're enjoying it.

00:06:18.639 --> 00:06:20.301
Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:06:20.301 --> 00:06:21.363
I believe in you.

00:06:21.363 --> 00:06:23.517
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:06:23.517 --> 00:06:25.249
and whatever your year one word is

00:06:25.249 --> 00:06:28.034
and I'll see you again tomorrow
morning for another shot

00:06:28.034 --> 00:06:28.889
of Espresso.

00:06:28.889 --> 00:06:31.524
♫ I wake up every morning

00:06:31.524 --> 00:06:34.051
